  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    Pass the Giggle ("the app") is a family party game for iPhone and iPad, developed by Matt Donders.
    This policy explains how the app handles your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>None.</strong> The app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
    <li>Does not connect to the internet to play</li>
    <li>Does not use analytics, crash reporting, or tracking</li>
    <li>Does not display advertisements or contain links out of the app</li>
    <li>Does not access your contacts, location, photos, camera, or microphone</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Player names, emoji and any cards you write are stored only on your device. They are never uploaded.
    Deleting the app removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The optional one-time unlock is handled entirely by Apple through the App Store. We never receive your
    payment details or Apple Account information. Purchases sit behind a grown-up check in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Pass the Giggle is made for families with young children. It does not collect personal information from
    anyone, including children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>Any changes to this policy will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Pass%20the%20Giggle%20Privacy">matt@mattdonders.com</a>.
  </p>
